<title>BELGIUM: European airport revenues, investment rise in 1995.</title>
<headline>European airport revenues, investment rise in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>European airports in 1995 generated $15.8 billion in revenues and reinvested 30 percent of that  -- or $4.8 billion -- in building facilities, the European section of the Airports Council International said Wednesday.</p>
<p>In 1995, revenue grew by 9.8 percent from the previous year, while investments grew by 5.5 percent, according to an ACI statement.</p>
<p>It added that the number of people employed at European airports, both directly and indirectly, increased slightly to 1.1 million in 1995.</p>
</text>
